==English==

===Etymology===
First recorded in the U.S.A. in the 18th century. The etymology is uncertain. Most probably a feminine form of [[Samuel]], possibly influenced by [[Anthea]]. Other suggestions include the Aramaic noun {{term|שמענתא|lang=arc|tr=šemʿanta||listener}} , from [[ܫܡܥ|ܫܡܥܬܐ]]. In India, Samantha can be interpreted as a variant spelling of {{term|Samanta}}, from the Sanskrit word meaning "universal, adjacent".
